I walk past the food stalls.
There I see a small shop.
There are beautiful ladles in the shop.
They are wooden ladles.
I take a ladle in my hand.
It is handmade.
The shopkeeper looks at me.
"What is the price of this?" I ask.
"That is four hundred and fifty rupees," he says.
Four hundred and fifty rupees!
That is a very high price.
I do not want it now.
I smile at him.
"It is too expensive," I say.
I gently put the ladle back.
He smiles and nods.
